.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-step-base 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-step\-base \- Print one `base <path> <id>` line per path, read at the merge base of HEAD and a ref
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten step base\fR [\fB\-\-ref\-env\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-ref\fR> <\fIpaths\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print one `base <path> <id>` line per path, read at the merge base of HEAD and a ref
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-ref\fR \fI<ref>\fR
The ref whose merge base with HEAD the lines are read at
.TP
\fB\-\-ref\-env\fR \fI<ref_env>\fR
A variable whose value, when set and non\-empty, replaces \-\-ref
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIpaths\fR>
The paths, after `\-\-`: one `base <path> <id>` line each, `absent` where missing
